 "lines": {
  "hook": "The sea is pulling you out. What's your first move?",
  "b1": "The beach shrinks, even though you're swimming hard toward it.",
  "b2": "A rip current flows out at up to eight feet per second.",
  "b3": "That's faster than an Olympic swimmer.",
  "b4": "Fighting it wears out even strong swimmers. That's how people drown.",
  "b5": "Here's the twist. It pulls you out, not under.",
  "b6": "One. Float. Let it carry you and save your energy.",
  "b7": "Two. Swim sideways, along the beach, until it lets go.",
  "b8": "Three. Still stuck? Float and wave so a lifeguard sees you.",
  "end": "Still swimming straight back? Float first, then save this."
 },
